=== runtime: struct patterns check only __struct__; @enforce_keys is construction-time only ===
pub_pat good: 7
pub_bare(%{total: 1})  (no check at all): {:ok, 1}
pub_pat(%{total: 1})   (head pattern refuses): {:error, FunctionClauseError}
via_pat(%{total: 1})   (def->defp: defp's own pattern refuses): {:error, FunctionClauseError}
via_bare(%{total: 1})  (def->defp bare: nothing refuses): {:ok, 1}
nested(%{item: %{total: 1}}) (defp pattern is the only check): {:error, FunctionClauseError}
pub_pat(%Order{id: 1}) via struct/2? bypass @enforce_keys:: {:ok, nil}
pub_pat(%{__struct__: Order, total: 9}) forged map accepted: {:ok, 9}
pub_int(1.5): {:error, FunctionClauseError}
field_int(%{qty: 1.5}) -> defp priv_int: {:ok, 3.0}
